                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: Heat flow through a two-layer brick wall held at 20 degC on one face and -5 degC on the other.
Fidelity: Engineering - transient conjugate heat transfer, not validated for this wall. Cite: Kastner and Dogan (SimAUD 2020).
Method: CHT Case solves conduction in two 0.15 m CHT Solid blocks of CHT Material Brick for 10000 s; unassigned faces stay adiabatic.
Result: Wall temperature T probed on a Brep Grid and drawn by Scalar Field Viewer; Live Residuals tracks convergence.
Needs: Eddy3D Setup &gt; Fully-coupled multi-region CFD / HAM / RAD / VEG (urbanMicroclimateFoam). Runtime: minutes.
Edit: Wall blocks, materials, boundary temperatures and simulated time.</item>
